# Front-End Dev-Mode: Error Recovery Implementation

## Purpose

This file provides specialized guidance for error recovery in front-end development. It focuses on identifying, diagnosing, and fixing critical errors in front-end applications, with emphasis on systematic error recovery patterns, fallback mechanisms, and robust error handling.

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file contains error recovery implementation patterns for front-end development and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in message-commands when implementing error recovery features:

```
dev-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/dev-mode/dev-mode-error-recovery.mdc
```

## Mode Activation

When activated with:

```
dev-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/dev-mode/dev-mode-error-recovery.mdc
```

This parameter enables:
- Comprehensive error diagnosis capabilities
- Structured error recovery workflows
- Fallback implementation patterns
- Graceful degradation approaches
- Error boundary implementations
- Retry mechanism strategies

## Implementation Strategy

The error recovery implementation strategy follows a structured approach:

### 1. Error Diagnosis Phase

Begin by identifying and diagnosing the specific errors to be addressed:

```typescript
// 1. Access error handling patterns
fetch_rules(["knowledge/patterns/impl/error-handling"], 
           "Understanding error handling patterns for front-end")

// 2. Check error logs
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path \"logs-main\" -Recurse -Filter \"*.log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"ERROR|Exception|failed\" | Select-Object -Last 20", false)

// 3. Analyze component errors
grep_search("throw|catch|Error|try", false, "*.tsx")

// 4. Check error boundary implementations
codebase_search("error boundary implementation", ["front-end/src/components"])

// 5. Examine API error handling
grep_search("catch.*error|onError|handleError", false, "*.tsx")
```

### 2. Implementation of Error Boundaries

Create or enhance error boundaries to catch and handle component errors:

```typescript
// 1. Create/update error boundary component
edit_file("front-end/src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx", 
          "Implement/enhance error boundary component",
          "// Error boundary component implementation\n" +
          "import React, { Component, ErrorInfo } from 'react';\n\n" +
          "interface ErrorBoundaryProps {\n" +
          "  fallback?: React.ReactNode;\n" +
          "  onError?: (error: Error, errorInfo: ErrorInfo) => void;\n" +
          "  children: React.ReactNode;\n" +
          "}\n\n" +
          "interface ErrorBoundaryState {\n" +
          "  hasError: boolean;\n" +
          "  error: Error | null;\n" +
          "}\n\n" +
          "class ErrorBoundary extends Component<ErrorBoundaryProps, ErrorBoundaryState> {\n" +
          "  constructor(props: ErrorBoundaryProps) {\n" +
          "    super(props);\n" +
          "    this.state = { hasError: false, error: null };\n" +
          "  }\n\n" +
          "  static getDerivedStateFromError(error: Error) {\n" +
          "    return { hasError: true, error };\n" +
          "  }\n\n" +
          "  componentDidCatch(error: Error, errorInfo: ErrorInfo) {\n" +
          "    console.error('ErrorBoundary caught an error', error, errorInfo);\n" +
          "    this.props.onError?.(error, errorInfo);\n" +
          "  }\n\n" +
          "  render() {\n" +
          "    if (this.state.hasError) {\n" +
          "      return this.props.fallback || (\n" +
          "        <div className=\"error-boundary-fallback\">\n" +
          "          <h2>Something went wrong.</h2>\n" +
          "          <details>\n" +
          "            <summary>Error Details</summary>\n" +
          "            <pre>{this.state.error?.toString()}</pre>\n" +
          "          </details>\n" +
          "        </div>\n" +
          "      );\n" +
          "    }\n\n" +
          "    return this.props.children;\n" +
          "  }\n" +
          "}\n\n" +
          "export default ErrorBoundary;")

